{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Any widow and orphan.</b> Any widow and orphan — a paradigm, like 'you shall not do any work and any image.' He mentioned the ger, who has no power, and afterward he mentioned the orphan and the widow, who are Israelites who have no power." "<b>You shall not afflict them.</b> This commandment is written in plural language, unlike all the laws written in this portion — because all are transgressors in them, even those who do not provoke, for they see their humiliation and remain silent and do not protest. And likewise he mentioned the punishment in plural language: 'and My anger shall wax hot and I will kill you,' etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:49.412007294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}